{
  "description": "Classical (Pavlovian) conditioning trial-runner — the learner runs CS+US pairing trials to drive an associative-strength curve toward its asymptote (acquisition), or runs CS-alone trials to drive it toward zero (extinction), via the Rescorla-Wagner rule plotted on a biology-canvas. Standalone by default; behind a lab router set matchMode and it renders only when MODE_SELECTED matches.",
  "ledger": {
    "entries": {
